    <section class="shell section--roomy">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="num">02 / The problem</span>
        <div>
          <h2>The notebook<br />in the rain.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-prose reveal" data-delay="1">
        <p>
          Urban researchers make their living noticing things on foot &mdash; how a
          street corner empties out at 4&nbsp;pm, where the cyclists actually go,
          who&rsquo;s photographed and who&rsquo;s ignored. The tools they used were a
          waterlogged Moleskine, an iPhone camera roll, a half-charged voice recorder,
          and three hours of cleanup back at the office.
        </p>
        <p>
          We did fourteen ride-alongs across Brooklyn, Mexico City, and Lisbon.
          Researchers needed: <strong>one-thumb capture</strong>, an interface that
          worked through a glove or a screen smudged with rain, and a way to find
          notes again that wasn&rsquo;t a search bar. The product had to be more
          forgiving than precise.
        </p>
      </div>

