    <section class="shell section--roomy">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="num">03 / The approach</span>
        <div>
          <h2>One thumb,<br />one big button, one map.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-prose reveal" data-delay="1">
        <p>
          We treated capture as the first job and everything else as cleanup. The
          home screen on Moraine is a map, with a single oversized capture button at
          the bottom &mdash; reachable with the thumb of the hand holding the phone,
          even with gloves. Tap captures a geotagged note. Press-and-hold starts a
          voice memo. Long-press lets you draw a quick sketch on the map.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Capture-first, organize-later.</strong> No folders, no required
            tags at the moment of capture. Cleanup is its own surface, used at home.</li>
          <li><strong>Geotemporal recall.</strong> &ldquo;Where I was last Tuesday at
            5&nbsp;pm&rdquo; should find a note faster than any search query.</li>
          <li><strong>Forgiving inputs.</strong> Voice transcription tolerates accents,
            background noise, and partial sentences. The app saves the audio file too,
            so the source of truth is always recoverable.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

