    <section class="shell section--roomy">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="num">04 / The design</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Built for the<br />wet, gloved, hurried hand.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-prose reveal" data-delay="1">
        <p>
          The capture button is 88&nbsp;pt across &mdash; deliberately bigger than
          Apple&rsquo;s recommendation. Map gestures use whole-thumb arcs, not
          two-finger pinches. Type sizes go up at night and in low light, automatically.
          Every interaction has a haptic confirmation that doesn&rsquo;t require
          looking at the screen.
        </p>
        <p>
          The cleanup surface is the slow counterpart: a long-form feed where you
          retag, transcribe, link, and write up. Researchers do this with coffee
          on Saturday morning. The feed knows that and shows up that way &mdash;
          unhurried, full of room to think.
        </p>
      </div>

